<title>DENMARK: FORECAST - Danish govt economic outlook 1998-2005.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Danish govt economic outlook 1998-2005.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a table of the main points from the Danish government's economic outlook for the period 1998-2005 announced on Wednesday (estimates from last Finance Ministry survey in December 1996 in middle and right-hand columns).</p>
<p>				1998-2005   1998-2000   2001-2005</p>
<p>Annual pct growth:</p>
<p>Private consumption	   2.6	   2.3	    2.5</p>
<p>Public sector expediture    1.0	   0.9	    1.1</p>
<p>Exports			   3.8	   4.2	    3.7</p>
<p>Imports			   3.9	   3.8	    4.0</p>
<p>GDP				 2.3	   2.5	    2.2</p>
<p>Inflation			 2.3	   2.3	    2.2</p>
<p>Hourly pay			3.8	   3.9	    3.8</p>
<p>Unemployment		    5.0	   7.1	    5.6</p>
<p>(1,000s workers)		149	   204	    165</p>
<p>Pct of GDP:</p>
<p>C/a surplus		     2.8	   2.0	    3.0</p>
<p>Govt public sector balance  3.3	   0.5	    2.4</p>
<p>Public debt			40	    50	     38</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
